# The members `get` and `set` are written in literals that are DESCRIPTORS: one held by a constant (its own layout, L1), two written in the map of Object.defineProperties, one of them under a computed key (the layout that all written descriptors share, L2). They run on the object defined upon, never on the descriptor: the literal is not written of their `this`.
